Development and test Ed25519 rental-token signing key, the PRIVATE half, read by
config/environments/{development,test}.rb. Fixed, so the known-answer test in
test/rental_token_issuer_test.rb, the firmware fixtures and the lock simulator agree.

DO NOT use in production: this file ships world-readable in a public repo, so
anyone with a clone could mint an unlock token every provisioned lock accepts —
bypassing reserve, pay, ownership and KYC. Production refuses to boot without an
explicit KIOSK_UNLOCK_SIGNING_KEY_PEM, and refuses this one.

An EARLIER dev keypair is in this repo's public git history and is therefore
burned: no lock should ever be provisioned with its public half (8857880d…).

Generated once: ruby -ropenssl -e "puts OpenSSL::PKey.generate_key('ED25519').private_to_pem"
(OpenSSL tolerates this text preamble when parsing the PEM below.)

-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
MC4CAQAwBQYDK2VwBCIEIEnP359Qh9fT7QlKLal2Tecb1CbAQvpxvo4EG8Sg7Asi
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
